 (** What the roster says about one keeper by name. An incomplete roster can
     only confirm presence, never absence. *)
 
+val liveness_reader : roster -> (string -> liveness)
+(** Prepare an immutable name lookup for repeated reads of this exact roster.
+    First observed rows and first errors win within their respective lists;
+    errors take precedence over observed rows, as in {!liveness_of_roster}.
+    Missing names retain the roster's complete/partial distinction. The reader
+    owns no mutable state and performs no I/O. A caller preparing one list uses
+    it only during that preparation, without retaining it as lifecycle authority
+    or reusing it after a new roster reading. *)
+
